    "description": "Long Beach Container Terminal operates an automated marine container terminal at the Port of Long Beach. Its customers include shipping lines, trucking operators, rail providers, and beneficial cargo owners moving import and export freight through Southern California. The operating model is asset-heavy and concession based, relying on large-scale terminal infrastructure, automated equipment, and throughput-linked port operations. Company materials state that the current Pier E facility opened in 2016, and Macquarie describes it as an automated terminal that plays a significant role in the Los Angeles-Long Beach port complex. A Macquarie-managed fund acquired LBCT in 2019, and Macquarie continues to position the asset around operating performance and decarbonization initiatives including the terminal’s Net Zero 2030 plan.",
